1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,815
Welcome to ResGrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,984 --> 00:00:06,596
In this lesson, we will automate a
repeatable task with visible outcomes.

3
00:00:06,814 --> 00:00:11,112
Manual copying between systems costs
time and hides failures when there

4
00:00:11,112 --> 00:00:13,290
is no recorded execution history.

5
00:00:13,426 --> 00:00:17,139
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:17,139 --> 00:00:19,251
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:20,078 --> 00:00:24,669
A workflow posts new calls to a team
channel, and a custom field records

8
00:00:24,670 --> 00:00:26,604
the fire district on each call.

9
00:00:26,799 --> 00:00:30,349
Automate repeated administrative
steps and connect ResGrid to

10
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:31,959
the other systems you use.

11
00:00:32,126 --> 00:00:36,105
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:36,106 --> 00:00:38,555
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:39,378 --> 00:00:43,000
Workflows, automations
triggered by department events.

14
00:00:43,243 --> 00:00:47,588
Start with one workflow for a task
you repeat and review its runs.

15
00:00:48,386 --> 00:00:53,650
User-defined fields, custom fields on
calls, personnel and other records.

16
00:00:53,867 --> 00:00:56,032
Add only the fields you must capture.

17
00:00:56,810 --> 00:00:59,085
API and MCP integrations.

18
00:00:59,295 --> 00:01:02,314
API and MCP access for other systems.

19
00:01:02,525 --> 00:01:06,576
Create credentials for each integration
and limit what they can access.

20
00:01:07,378 --> 00:01:08,342
New workflow.

21
00:01:08,548 --> 00:01:10,462
Create an automation workflow.

22
00:01:10,687 --> 00:01:14,100
Have the destination systems
and credentials ready and

23
00:01:14,101 --> 00:01:15,988
decide who owns each automation.

24
00:01:16,797 --> 00:01:17,830
Workflow runs.

25
00:01:18,048 --> 00:01:21,326
The history of workflow
runs, including failures.

26
00:01:21,564 --> 00:01:24,977
Have the destination systems
and credentials ready and

27
00:01:24,978 --> 00:01:26,859
decide who owns each automation.

28
00:01:27,649 --> 00:01:29,472
Import and migration planning.

29
00:01:29,689 --> 00:01:32,864
Plan moving your data from
another system into ResGrid.

30
00:01:33,087 --> 00:01:36,499
Have the destination systems
and credentials ready and

31
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,382
decide who owns each automation.

32
00:01:39,218 --> 00:01:42,112
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

33
00:01:42,335 --> 00:01:46,807
Step one, choose one event and an
approved destination for a workflow.

34
00:01:47,055 --> 00:01:52,763
Step two, configure the workflow action,
data mapping, and integration access.

35
00:01:53,002 --> 00:01:56,832
Step three, trigger a controlled
demo event and review workflow

36
00:01:56,848 --> 00:01:58,631
runs for success or failure.

37
00:01:59,436 --> 00:02:01,065
Now verify the result.

38
00:02:01,304 --> 00:02:05,687
Confirm the intended action at the
destination and inspect the recorded run.

39
00:02:05,919 --> 00:02:09,411
Test a controlled failure and
document who owns retries.

40
00:02:09,604 --> 00:02:13,847
A common problem to watch for,
a saved workflow is not evidence

41
00:02:13,849 --> 00:02:16,001
that its destination received data.

42
00:02:16,198 --> 00:02:20,119
Protected content requires the
separately reviewed egress path.

43
00:02:20,903 --> 00:02:22,734
Your practice task is simple.

44
00:02:22,911 --> 00:02:26,484
Create a demo-only new call
workflow and inspect its run.

45
00:02:26,682 --> 00:02:32,021
Record successful and failed execution
evidence, owner, and recovery steps.

46
00:02:32,215 --> 00:02:36,731
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

47
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:40,829
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
